WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.533
Agentic Stream turns sensor readings into safe, governed action.

2
00:00:06.283 --> 00:00:11.517
Here is one real recorded run, with a simulator playing the sensor and the device.

3
00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:15.822
Let's follow it from a warming sensor to a verified effect.

4
00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:19.801
A temperature sensor is warming up.

5
00:00:21.201 --> 00:00:27.100
At the edge, each reading becomes an event, with an identity and the time it really happened.

6
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:36.175
Ingress checks each event against its schema, then appends it to a log that is never rewritten.

7
00:00:37.575 --> 00:00:39.995
Malformed input would be quarantined.

8
00:00:41.395 --> 00:00:44.615
An event is evidence, never an instruction.

9
00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:52.331
The stream engine works in event time: when a reading happened, not when it arrived.

10
00:00:53.281 --> 00:00:59.791
A watermark trails the newest reading by fifteen seconds, and marks how far time has safely advanced.

11
00:01:00.741 --> 00:01:03.725
A late reading still lands at its true time.

12
00:01:05.125 --> 00:01:12.515
A five-minute window slides every thirty seconds, and operators turn it into features: the mean, and the slope.

13
00:01:13.565 --> 00:01:15.747
Same input, same features.

14
00:01:17.947 --> 00:01:22.726
Features update a Situation: the durable record of one condition.

15
00:01:23.576 --> 00:01:27.471
A phase changes only when its rule holds for a minimum time.

16
00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:35.998
After a minute, it moved from candidate to watch. Thirty seconds later, to cooling, meaning cooling is needed.

17
00:01:37.248 --> 00:01:41.820
Each window step publishes a provisional version, then an on-time one.

18
00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:46.127
Twenty-two versions, and none can be edited.

19
00:01:48.727 --> 00:01:54.871
Reasoning is slow and costly, so a deterministic scheduler decides when it is worth it.

20
00:01:55.721 --> 00:01:58.380
The four candidate versions fail the trigger.

21
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.422
Version five passes, and is queued.

22
00:02:03.772 --> 00:02:06.734
Version seven scores higher, and replaces it.

23
00:02:08.134 --> 00:02:13.595
The other sixteen bring nothing new, so they are ignored, each with a recorded reason.

24
00:02:14.845 --> 00:02:19.268
Twenty-two versions, one episode. No model call per event.

25
00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:25.929
Admission opens one episode: a bounded reasoning session.

26
00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:33.155
It is rebound to the newest snapshot, version twenty-two, and that snapshot never changes.

27
00:02:34.405 --> 00:02:38.146
A deadline, a budget, and a fence number keep it bounded.

28
00:02:39.396 --> 00:02:43.282
Tamoz, the reasoner, runs in a separate worker process.

29
00:02:44.132 --> 00:02:48.670
It reads evidence, and can only propose. It cannot act.

30
00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:58.101
Tamoz returns a typed decision: a rising over-temperature, at ninety-six percent confidence.

31
00:02:58.951 --> 00:03:02.943
It proposes one intent: set the indicator to alert.

32
00:03:04.193 --> 00:03:10.493
The validator accepts only what the spec's catalog allows. An unknown intent would be refused.

33
00:03:11.743 --> 00:03:13.711
This one passes every check.

34
00:03:16.311 --> 00:03:20.814
Policy checks again, against the current state, right before dispatch.

35
00:03:22.214 --> 00:03:26.186
The indicator is low risk, so it is approved automatically.

36
00:03:27.436 --> 00:03:31.898
A fan, class R2, would wait for a signed human approval.

37
00:03:32.748 --> 00:03:36.340
That path is designed, but was not part of this run.

38
00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:44.205
The command gets a stable idempotency key, and is written to an outbox before it is sent.

39
00:03:45.055 --> 00:03:50.260
So a crash cannot lose it, and a retry is recognised as the same request.

40
00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:55.236
It goes out through the device gateway, and the indicator switches on.

41
00:03:56.586 --> 00:04:01.732
Three answers come back: a receipt, a result, and a state query.

42
00:04:02.982 --> 00:04:06.797
Only when the observed state matches is the effect verified.

43
00:04:09.397 --> 00:04:16.808
Sixty-one events, twenty-two versions, one episode, one decision, one verified effect.

44
00:04:17.858 --> 00:04:22.705
Every step left a durable record, so every outcome can be explained.

45
00:04:23.755 --> 00:04:26.761
And new readings keep flowing into the same loop.
